{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_entry_mc24_three_excluded_forms", "label": "Three Excluded Forms (sums, differences, symmetric bounds)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/entry-MC24.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every coupling axis's exact ceiling is symmetric under particle-hole conjugation, and a symmetric non-constant function is not monotone, so the admissibility condition cannot carry it. Hence coupling bounds are permanently envelopes, not a temporary weakness of the construction."}, {"id": "recovered_entry_mc24_symmetric_bounds", "label": "Symmetric Bounds under Particle-Hole Conjugation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/entry-MC24.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_entry_mc24_envelope_gap_decomposition", "label": "Envelope Gap: Reflection, Congruence, Triangle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/entry-MC24.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_entry_mc24_half_triangle_join_closure", "label": "The Join-Closed, Meet-Broken Half-Triangle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/entry-MC24.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "{|2L\u22122S| \u2264 2J \u2264 2L+2S} closes under join at caps 6, 8, 10, 12 and fails meets by 2,862 / 12,489 / 40,887 / 110,229 \u2014 certainty surviving upward and dying downward, the reflection asymmetry stated as an inequality. Imposing the parity congruence kills the join closure too (1,848 failures at cap 6), so the surviving half belongs to the parity-free triangle and nothing larger."}, {"id": "recovered_entry_mc24_admissibility_condition", "label": "Admissibility Condition (single-parent monotone bound)", "file_type": "